  "semantics": [
    "Frontend restore1400851d0 loads Save145a8c900, takes optional Pick or default145a99de0, calls domain normalization145a98160 then account clamp145a8b4c0 and randomizes exact Hero placeholder before installation.",
    "Command11 native dispatch selector11 maps to table index9; signed relative slot146fbb9e0 targets145b1bd86. Original instructions, not unexpanded raw Ghidra switch, establish this route.",
    "Command11 calls domain normalization145a98160 then account clamp145a8b4c0 with server Save+1020. Normalized Pick becomes live server+1220; its eight-byte Hero at+1258 replaces matching class in Save heroes(+168/+170/+178) or appends before save writer145a92f00.",
    "Stock packet ordinal0x3d maps to table index7, slot146fbb9a0, branch145b1396e. The selected branch receives decoded GUID bytes then invokes roster factory145b1b5c0.",
    "Selection compares only row+18 GUID, copies matching56-byte record identity, and assigns GUID to server+17c8. The two bounded selection ranges preserve all72 ordinary race/class pairs without inspecting account purchase eligibility. Stops before zone/run construction."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Raw Ghidra ranges have generic ABI, no PE globals/prototypes and can expand common packet tails; exact original instruction ranges and the retained selector slots define the admitted contracts.",
    "Raw account-command pseudocode stops at an unexpanded switch. Its recorded selector11 slot and exact original branch instructions establish only command11, not other command ordinals.",
    "Roster replay supplies one synthetic typed56-byte row, decoded GUID1, a no-op deallocation seam and one connection. It stops after selected GUID/identity commit, before zone/run construction.",
    "All72 supported ordinary race/class pairs survive that original selection path. Invalid race/class input behavior and full client/server login protocol are outside this proof.",
    "No Rust compilation, game/server/client process execution, actual filesystem/network effects or original/rebuilt parity."
  ],
